// The golden scenes (spec §9 gate 3; M4 R1): what `cargo xtask golden` captures with the sandbox and compares
// with `<name>.<family>.png` beside this file. `sapphire_testkit`'s `scenes` module reads it, and its tests
// hold it whole: it parses, names are unique, each scene has its Metal golden, every PNG here belongs to a
// scene, and a scene with lavapipe's and WARP's goldens has their CI times.
//
// A scene is the sandbox's `--capture <png>` with:
// - `name`: the goldens' file stem, lowercase letters and hyphens.
// - `size`: the capture's size in pixels, `640x360` (small enough for lavapipe and WARP) unless it says
//   another, as the HUD and screen scenes do for their aspect ratios.
// - `ticks`: the simulation tick the capture is taken at (`--capture-ticks`).
// - `base`: the name of one of `bases`, arguments several scenes share, which come before its own.
// - `args`: the rest of the sandbox's command line: what the scene shows, and the pins that hold off what it
//   doesn't. A path under `tests/` (a replay, a save) is found from this directory.
// - `gates`: FLIP gates of its own, where the default (mean 0.01, p99 0.12, worst 16×16 tile 0.15;
//   `golden.rs`) isn't the one: `mean`, `percentile`, `percentile_max`, `worst_tile`.
// - `ci_seconds`: its median wall time in seconds in CI's golden jobs on lavapipe and WARP, which `--shard`
//   splits their scenes by. A scene without it counts as the costliest on both, so a new one never lands on a
//   full shard.
//
// A new golden is a row here and its Metal PNG (`cargo xtask golden --update --scene <name>`). Its first CI
// run fails on the missing lavapipe and WARP goldens and uploads their captures with each shard's
// `timings.json`: the commit that takes the captures takes the scene's `ci_seconds` from the same run. To
// refresh every scene's times, take the medians of at least three recent runs on `main` (`gh run download
// <run> -p 'golden-dx12-warp-*' -p 'golden-vulkan-lavapipe-*'`), since runners vary too much for one: I1's
// three runs' lavapipe totals were 2835 to 4260 s and WARP's 5603 to 7386 s. The times here are the medians
// of runs 42772431295, 42790087819 and 42799339433 (d684625, 4fe253e and 0755aaf; M4 I1). The 117 scenes
// those runs didn't have (M4 R1) take the medians of runs 43060916318, 43001302260 and 42954179184 (d8b621cc
// and d98cf1a9) where all three had them, and run 43060916318's own times for the 81 only it had.
//
// Keep one scene to a block, in the order they were added, each after the ones before it: a scene from before
// a feature pins it off, so its golden stays byte-identical when the feature lands.
//
// Those from before the sky's layers (M1 W2) pin the sky's gradient alone, `--plain-sky` (no discs, glows,
// stars or clouds): they are about the character, and the sky has scenes of its own. Those from before
// temporal AA (M1 R7) pin 4× MSAA (`--aa msaa`), which the desktop tiers drew with until then. Those from
// before post's compositing layers (M1 P2) pin post as it was, `--plain-post` (no diffusion glow, character
// bloom, gradient layers, lens flare or vignette tint), which the post scenes show; the environment's (M1 W4)
// among them, which draw the world as the desktop tiers do, under the whole sky and temporal AA. The outline
// scenes (M1 C4) pin all three, so they show the lines alone. Those from before shadows (M1 R4), the post and
// outline scenes included, pin them off (`--shadows off`, the player's quality setting). The shadow scenes
// pin their tier, whose shadows they show (the golden runners select Desktop-Low by device), and plain post,
// so they show shadows alone. The screen effect scenes (M1 P3) push the sample presets held on one frame
// (`--post-effect <preset>@<seconds>`) over the full look; no earlier scene pushes any, and an empty effect
// stack draws exactly what it drew before, so nothing earlier needs pinning. Every scene from before fog (M1
// W3) pins it off (`--fog off`: no fog in any frame and no fog cards in the courtyard); the fog scenes pin
// plain post and no shadows, so they show fog alone. The rim and hair scenes (M1 C5) pin the plain sky and
// post, 4× MSAA, no shadows and no fog, so they show the character prepass's readers alone. The foliage
// scenes (M1 W6) plant the foliage samples in the courtyard (`--foliage <view>`; no earlier scene plants any,
// and the wind is calm without it) and pin plain post and no fog, so they show foliage alone, its shadows on.
// Every scene from before ambient occlusion (M1 W5), the screen effect, fog, rim, hair and foliage scenes
// included, pins it off (`--ao off`, the player's quality setting), and none of them loads a probe grid, so
// the ambient hemisphere lights them all as before. The ambient scenes (W5) pin their tier, plain post and no
// fog, so they show the probe grid and ambient occlusion with the tier's shadows; the grid is the desktop
// cook's, which the runner loads on every backend. The night scenes with characters (`turntable-night`,
// `sky-night`, `environment-night`, `fog-night`, `ambient-night` and `ambient-capsule`) changed with the
// night character light fix, which retuned the default day's night character key; `night-character` draws a
// character at night under the whole look, which no scene did before, with ambient occlusion off and no probe
// grid like every scene but W5's.
//
// The look-dev scenes (M1 X1) pin Desktop-High, the tier whose look they judge, and ambient occlusion off, as
// every scene but W5's: every other landed feature draws in them, as a game would. They run on the stage's
// own day (`content/lookdev/lookdev_day.ron`, X1 part 2), which only `--look-dev` loads, and plant its
// foliage, so no other scene sees either. The stylized GI scenes (M1 C2's follow-up) light the face rig by
// the character light rig's GI alone, its key light off (`--face-layout gi` and `gi-clamped`), at hours whose
// keys the night character light fix leaves as they were (17:30 and 10:00), and pin what the face scenes pin,
// so they show the GI alone: each of its steps (the sphere and the camera bias on the GI's normals, the HSV
// clamp's saturation and value, the skin tint, the occlusion) fails one of them when broken. The eye scenes
// (M1 C6) pin what the rim and hair scenes pin, AO off among it, so they show the eye layers alone, but for
// the highlight's, which draws post's glow and bloom over its glint. The debug view scenes (M1 F5) alone set
// a view (`--debug-view <view>`; off, every other scene's, builds and draws nothing, so nothing earlier needs
// pinning) and pin plain post, no shadows and AO off, so the frame they draw over changes only with what they
// show; the wireframe and overdraw keep fog for its cards. The material layer scenes (M1 C7) place the layer
// samples beside the character (`--materials`; no earlier scene places any, and every layer is off in every
// earlier material) and pin 4× MSAA, no shadows, no fog and no AO, so they show the layers alone; the fade
// scenes fade the character (`--fade`; no earlier scene fades one) in the courtyard under plain post, AO off,
// through temporal AA and through MSAA.
//
// The character shading follow-up scenes (M1 C8) turn one of its features on each, all off by default, so no
// earlier scene draws any: the two-sided garments (`--two-sided`) pin what the material layer scenes pin; the
// shadow hue scenes (`--shade-hue`) light the face rig at golden hour, with and without the hue, and pin what
// the face scenes pin; the folded rim scenes light the rim scenes' figures from behind through the gameplay
// rig's limits (`--rim-rig folded`), with and without a camera rim (`--camera-rim`), and pin what the rim
// scenes pin; the soft bangs' shadow scene softens the face rig's faces (`--hair-shadow-softness`) under the
// hair scene's keys and pins what it pins; the back-lit hair scenes light the face rig from behind
// (`--face-layout backlit`), without and with light through the hair (`--hair-transmission`), and pin what
// the hair scenes pin.
//
// The debug draw scene (M2 T1) alone turns debug draw on (`--debug-draw`; nothing else in these builds draws
// any, so no earlier scene changes) and pins what the material layer scenes pin, with plain post and a plain
// sky, so the frame under its lines changes only with what they show. Its view of a fight
// (`debugdraw-volumes`) plays a committed replay, which the app checks against the checksums beside it before
// it writes the picture.
//
// The effects scenes (M2 E2) play `--vfx`'s shows at fixed ticks, whose simulation is seeded: the sword arc
// at noon and at night, a hit at sunset and a duel's worst moment, on the look-dev stage under temporal AA
// and at Mobile-Low, then alone with everything else pinned off.
//
// The combat HUD scenes (M2 I2) alone draw the on-screen interface (`--hud fixed`, one frozen frame on a
// made-up clock; no other scene has any, and a frame with no quads builds and draws nothing, so nothing
// earlier needs pinning), over the look-dev stage, pinned as its scenes are but with 4× MSAA in place of
// temporal AA, which needs no warm-up frames: the backdrop is a backdrop. Their `size` sets each one's aspect
// ratio. `hud-energy-*` add the player's ultimate (`--hud-energy`, M3 Q3c), its meter empty and full, on the
// wide frame and on the iPhone's.
//
// The moving character's scenes (M2 N2) play a clip on the look-dev character (`--clip`; no earlier scene
// plays one, and a character without a clip is never sampled) and pin what the look-dev scenes pin.
//
// The arena scenes (M2 O5) pin what the look-dev scenes pin: Desktop-High and ambient occlusion off, and the
// plain camera (`--arena-shot follow`), so tuning the camera director moves none of them. They alone run
// `--arena`, so no earlier scene sees its stage. `arena-replay` plays a replay on it, and
// `arena-fight-telegraph`, `arena-fight-hit`, `arena-fight-cut` and `arena-fight-slash` a fight with the
// enemy (M2 G6), side on, so the character isn't in front of what they're there to show. `arena-party-second`
// and `arena-party-third` play a party's fight (M2 G7), and only they and `game-hud-party-*` run `--party`. `cutscene-gate-*` stand
// the arena's stage in the Lantern Ward's court for a replay that watches its gate cutscene (M3 Q3), and only
// they play a cutscene from a fight. `arena-ultimate-chop` plays the player's ultimate (M3 Q3b) on the
// arena's own stage, the only scene in a move's cinematic. `arena-skirmish` plays eight fighters (M3 B1), on
// the director. `arena-boss` plays a boss (M3 B3), just past the phase where it enrages, with its bar and
// phase marks. `arena-captain` draws two kinds of enemy at once, each as itself (M3 B3b).
// `color-vision-telegraph` alone shows the colour-vision view (`--color-vision`, M4 A5; off, every other
// scene's, builds and draws nothing): an enemy's wind-up and its mark as a deuteranope sees them.
//
// The tier scenes (M4 T0) draw three shots as each tier ships, AO and all, at the tier's own scale and at its
// dynamic floor: the face's close-up on every tier, and the ward's street and a hit's post on the low tiers.
// The phone tiers' set a `size`, as the HUD scenes do, a phone's shape, and draw at the scales a 1170-row
// phone draws, so their bilinear upscale is a phone's. They pin nothing else, and keep their frames few, for
// the CPU rasterizers.
//
// The display text scenes (M3 U8) draw a title in the display face at four sizes over the HUD scenes' night
// street, pinned as those are, the smaller two from the glyph pages and the larger two from the face's cooked
// field: Oxanium at one pixel to the point, and Dela Gothic One at three, as a phone's capture is. They alone
// run `--display-text`, and they draw the interface as the HUD scenes do.
//
// The driven material scenes (M5 L11) alone drive a character's materials (`--dissolve`, `--flash`,
// `--emission-scale`; nothing driven, every other scene's, draws exactly as before) or place the glass
// samples (`--glass`; no earlier material has a see-through region or glass), in the courtyard under temporal
// AA at Desktop-High with AO and fog off, as the fade scenes stand.
(
    type: "sapphire::testkit::GoldenScenes",
    version: 1,
    data: (
        bases: {
            // A game screen's golden (M3 U7): on a flat color, so it stays cheap and moves only for what it
            // shows, with its screen (`--ui-game`) and language (`--ui-locale`) after it. The title's version
            // label is pinned (0.1.0), a packaged build's longer form, so a new version moves no golden.
            "game-screen": ["--tier", "desktop-high", "--plain-sky", "--plain-post", "--aa", "msaa",
                            "--ao", "off", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ui-plain",
                            "--ui-version", "v0.1.0 (1234)"],
            // The court gate's cutscene in the game as it ships (M3 Q4), with its language
            // (`--game-language`) after it: a continue from `ward-gate.progress.ron` walks back through the
            // gate, into the cutscene at frame 17, and tick 251, 3.9 s on, falls mid-way through the warden's
            // line (2.9 to 4.9 s). The 160 frames before 161 are drawn a tenth as wide and high
            // (`--game-draw-from 161`, after the language), so a software rasterizer draws 91 frames at full
            // size, not 251. The cutscene's cut at 2.5 s, frame 166, drops TAA's history as the size changing
            // does, so the last frame is byte for byte the one drawing them all would give; drawing full size
            // from 167 on isn't.
            "ward-gate": ["--tier", "desktop-high", "--game", "continue",
                          "--progress", "tests/saves/ward-gate.progress.ron", "--game-forward"],
        },
        scenes: [
            (
                name: "turntable-start",
                ticks: 0,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off",
                       "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 5.0, warp: 1.7),
            ),
            (
                name: "turntable",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off",
                       "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.4, warp: 1.8),
            ),
            // Without MSAA or TAA every outline and terminator edge is a hard pixel step, the case
            // most sensitive to precision differences.
            (
                name: "turntable-msaa-off",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--aa", "off", "--plain-sky", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off",
                       "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 3.6, warp: 1.7),
            ),
            // Three colored local lights through the clustered path (M1 R5): their splits on the
            // head and arm, and a spot's pool on the pedestal.
            (
                name: "turntable-lights",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--lights", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.6, warp: 1.5),
            ),
            // The scene at render scale 0.7 (448×252), upsampled by post's final pass (M1 R6).
            (
                name: "turntable-render-scale",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--render-scale", "0.7", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.5, warp: 1.4),
            ),
            // The procedural stalk beside the character (M1 R2): compute skinning bends it and its
            // two morph targets swell its top and narrow its middle, drawn from its skinning outputs
            // with shading and outline.
            (
                name: "turntable-skinned",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--skinned", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.6, warp: 1.8),
            ),
            // Sunset from the default day (M1 W1), between its golden-hour and sunset keys: a low
            // orange key light from the right, the sky's horizon band, violet-tinted shade and
            // post's two grading LUTs blended (80% toward sunset's).
            (
                name: "turntable-sunset",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--time-of-day", "18.5", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.4, warp: 2.0),
            ),
            // The anime character shader swatches beside the character (M1 C1): ramp mode over the
            // cooked swatch ramp and control map (per-ID rows, a striped shadow bias, a painted
            // shadow), the same with a subsurface mix, and three bands in per-ID colors from vertex
            // material IDs.
            (
                name: "turntable-swatches",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--swatches", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.5, warp: 1.5),
            ),
            // Night from the default day (M1 C2), halfway from dusk to midnight: the character lit by
            // its light rig's key (time of day's character key, brighter than the world's moon, from
            // the moon high on the camera's left) and stylized GI under a deep blue ambient, against
            // the night sky and two blended grading LUTs.
            (
                name: "turntable-night",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--time-of-day", "22", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.4, warp: 1.7),
            ),
            // The face look-dev rig (M1 C3): the cooked face test head in two rows, each lit by the
            // key light from its own angle in head space. A yaw sweep from 135° on the heads' right
            // round to 135° on their left (mirror-image SDF shadows, eyes and brows lit), then a top
            // light, light from above and to the side, a blush, and a gloom with a blush.
            (
                name: "faces",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--faces", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 7.8, warp: 4.5),
            ),
            // The sky by day (M1 W2), looking up past the character toward the morning sun: its
            // white-hot disc and wide glow, cirrus streaks overhead, and the card clouds' band on the
            // horizon, two-tone (white tops over lavender shade) with a rim, at 9:00's coverage.
            (
                name: "sky-day",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--time-of-day", "9", "--view", "99,-22", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.0, warp: 1.8),
            ),
            // Sunset (M1 W2): the sun low in a gap of the card clouds, its glow spread along the
            // horizon, gold-lit clouds over violet shade with bright rims toward the sun, and cirrus
            // catching the color.
            (
                name: "sky-sunset",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--time-of-day", "18.5", "--view", "-100,-6", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.7, warp: 1.8),
            ),
            // Night (M1 W2): the moon's disc and halo, procedural stars and the Milky Way on the
            // turning celestial sphere, and dark clouds with moonlit rims.
            (
                name: "sky-night",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--time-of-day", "21", "--view", "112,-20", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.7, warp: 2.0),
            ),
            // Temporal AA (M1 R7), the desktop tiers' antialiasing: the turntable held still while
            // 32 jittered frames converge, so outlines and light splits are antialiased as 4× MSAA
            // draws them.
            (
                name: "turntable-taa",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--aa", "taa", "--capture-frames", "32", "--plain-sky",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                // `turntable-taa` and `turntable-taa-upsampled` allow a mean of 0.0065, where the default
                // allows 0.01 (review DV-2). They differ only in `--render-scale 0.667`, which the second
                // exists to show, and read as each other they stay inside every default gate on every family:
                // mean 0.0085 to 0.0095, p99 0.066, worst tile 0.063. Their own noise leaves room for this
                // one gate: at most 0.0046 on lavapipe, 0.0005 on Metal and none on WARP. The mean separates
                // them best: 0.0046 from 0.0085, where the p99 and the worst tile have 0.044 from 0.062.
                gates: (mean: 0.0065),
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 2.0, warp: 5.2),
            ),
            // The turntable spinning at 3 rad/s, about 8 times its usual speed, for the 32 frames up
            // to the capture: outlines and two-tone edges must follow without ghost trails or smears.
            (
                name: "turntable-taa-motion",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--aa", "taa", "--spin", "3", "--capture-frames", "32",
                       "--capture-step", "1", "--plain-sky", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off",
                       "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.4, warp: 6.3),
            ),
            // Temporal upsampling: the scene at two thirds of the output's size (427×240), resolved
            // to 640×360 over 32 still frames.
            (
                name: "turntable-taa-upsampled",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--aa", "taa", "--render-scale", "0.667", "--capture-frames", "32",
                       "--plain-sky", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                gates: (mean: 0.0065),
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.1, warp: 5.6),
            ),
            // The environment shader (M1 W4) by day: the character in the courtyard, under the morning
            // sun from the front left. Painted ground, a colonnade receding into rolling hills, a
            // plaster wall and boulders: soft wrapped light, lavender shadow sides with a warm band
            // along the pillars' terminators, terminators softening and colors greying with
            // distance, and the character reading on top.
            (
                name: "environment-day",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--environment", "--aa", "taa", "--capture-frames", "32",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 6.3, warp: 12.1),
            ),
            // Sunset (18:30): the low orange sun from the right warms every lit face, the shadow
            // sides keep time of day's violet tint, and the lanterns begin to glow.
            (
                name: "environment-sunset",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--environment", "--time-of-day", "18.5", "--aa", "taa",
                       "--capture-frames", "32", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 4.6, warp: 10.5),
            ),
            // Night (22:00): the world under the moon and a deep blue ambient, the lanterns glowing
            // orange, and the demo lights' pools on the ground and the pedestal (local lights through
            // both families' shaders), the character lit by its own rig's brighter key.
            (
                name: "environment-night",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--plain-post", "--environment", "--time-of-day", "22", "--lights", "--aa", "taa",
                       "--capture-frames", "32", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 6.9, warp: 13.7),
            ),
            // Post's compositing layers by day (M1 P2), through temporal AA as the desktop tiers draw:
            // the diffusion glow softening the clouds, the top of the frame deepened toward the sky's
            // blue, the ground's shade toward the bottom, a soft pool of light on the character, whose
            // own bloom is held back (the character mask).
            (
                name: "post-day",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--time-of-day", "10", "--aa", "taa", "--capture-frames", "32", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 4.4, warp: 9.7),
            ),
            // Sunset through Mobile-Low's fused pass (4× MSAA, four bloom levels): a warm, dreamy
            // glow over the clouds and along the horizon, violet from above, the ground in a deep
            // violet shade below, the character crisp in front of it.
            (
                name: "post-sunset",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--time-of-day", "18.5", "--tier", "mobile-low", "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off",
                       "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.4, warp: 2.4),
            ),
            // The lens flare: the sunset sun in view beside the character, its warm ring and streak,
            // colored ghosts down the axis through the middle of the frame, and the diffusion glow
            // around the sun.
            (
                name: "post-flare",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--time-of-day", "18.5", "--view", "-100,-6", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 1.2, warp: 2.5),
            ),
            // Outline width over distance (M1 C4): more of the character from 4 m to 90 m behind it,
            // seen from nearly level. Their lines thin along the width's two-segment curve, hold
            // their width in the world far away, and are gone on the last, past the LOD cutoff.
            (
                name: "outlines-distance",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--outline-row", "--plain-post", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa", "--shadows", "off",
                       "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.5, warp: 1.5),
            ),
            // The same row through a 20° lens from farther away, the character framed as before:
            // its lines keep their width, and the row's, nearer in effective distance, widen.
            (
                name: "outlines-telephoto",
                ticks: 90,
                args: ["--outline-row", "--fov", "20", "--plain-post", "--plain-sky", "--aa", "msaa",
                       "--shadows", "off", "--fog", "off", "--ao", "off"],
                ci_seconds: (lavapipe: 0.4, warp: 1.5),
            ),
            // The hard-edged sample (M1 C4): flat-shaded shapes with every edge split, whose cooked
